    {
      "type": "indie-mag-single-column",
      "title": "From the NFL Community",
      "items": [
        {
          "title": "The Imagination Gap",
          "description": "<p style=\"margin: 0 0 16px 0; padding: 0;    ; font-family: Domine, serif !important; font-size: 17px !important; line-height: 1.5 !important; color: #111111 !important; text-align: left !important\">Back in Office Hours Side Projects Edition N°280, Pawel Halicki shared a thought-provoking reflection on the challenges organizations face in strategic thinking and future planning — and what to do about it.</p>\n<p style=\"margin: 0 0 16px 0; padding: 0;    ; font-family: Domine, serif !important; font-size: 17px !important; line-height: 1.5 !important; color: #111111 !important; text-align: left !important\">Pawel reminded us that 96% of senior leaders lack time for straegic thinking, while the feeling is that the future arrives faster than ever — so faster than one can adopt strategy. So if you don't have a structured way to explore the future, you risk being left behind.</p>\n<p style=\"margin: 0 0 16px 0; padding: 0;    ; font-family: Domine, serif !important; font-size: 17px !important; line-height: 1.5 !important; color: #111111 !important; text-align: left !important\">Is imagination the missing link? Pawel suggests that cultivating imagination within organizations is key to bridging this gap. By fostering a culture that encourages creative thinking and speculative exploration, organizations can better anticipate and adapt to future challenges.</p>",
          "image": "https://imagedelivery.net/gaLGizR3kCgx5yRLtiRIOw/04198323-f91b-4dda-1158-6c4aa62e3500/w=600",
          "link": "https://www.figma.com/proto/6vF1ijJvTupqR8T2d68JKx/Practical-Futures-Intro---Near-Future-Lab?page-id=0%3A1&node-id=2-305&viewport=45%2C388%2C0.04&t=plNj4iyPQ1f4338O-1&scaling=contain&content-scaling=fixed/"
        }
      ],
      "containerStyles": {
        "backgroundColor": null,
        "padding": "15px 20px",
        "borderRadius": "0px"
      }
    },
