        {
          "title": "This again..",
          "category": "YOU JUDGE",
          "description": "<p style=\"margin: 0 0 16px 0; padding: 0;    ; font-family: IBM Plex Sans, sans-serif !important; font-size: 17px !important; line-height: 1.2 !important; color: #111111 !important; text-align: left !important\">James Padolsey exposes the fragility of using Large Language Models in decision-making, revealing how even minor tweaks in prompts can drastically alter outcomes. His insights into the biases inherent in AI evaluations raise serious concerns about the reliability of these models in critical areas like hiring and law.</p>",
          "channel": "the-dept-of-what?",
          "link": "https://www.cip.org/blog/llm-judges-are-unreliable"
        },
        {
          "title": "Implications of A.I. in storytelling",
          "category": "REAL FICTION",
          "description": "<p style=\"margin: 0 0 16px 0; padding: 0;    ; font-family: IBM Plex Sans, sans-serif !important; font-size: 17px !important; line-height: 1.2 !important; color: #111111 !important; text-align: left !important\">A.I. is making waves in Hollywood, from 'The Morning Show' to 'Black Mirror,' yet the industry seems oblivious to the ethical quagmire it creates. As labor disputes highlight A.I.'s encroachment on creative jobs, the gap between fiction and reality widens, leaving us to ponder the true cost of this technology.</p>",
